# Visual Content Guide

## Philosophy

**Diagrams are not decoration. They are explanation.**

Before finalizing any post, ask yourself:
+ What concept would be clearer as a diagram?
+ Am I explaining a process, loop, comparison, or hierarchy?
+ Would a visual model help readers grasp this faster?

If yes to any of these, create a diagram.

---

## When to Use Diagrams

| Scenario | Diagram Type | Example Use Case |
|----------|--------------|------------------|
| **Process or workflow** | Flowchart (`graph TD`) | User authentication flow, build pipeline |
| **Decision tree** | Flowchart with conditionals | Algorithm logic, conditional routing |
| **Loop or cycle** | Graph with back-edges | Habit loops, feedback cycles, retry logic |
| **Comparison** | Side-by-side nodes | REST vs GraphQL, junior vs senior mindset |
| **Timeline or sequence** | Left-to-right flow (`graph LR`) | Project phases, evolution of a concept |
| **Hierarchy** | Tree structure | Class inheritance, organizational structure |

---

## Diagram Templates

### 1. Simple Process Flow

```mermaid
graph TD
    Start["<b>Start Point</b><br/><i>Initial state</i>"]
    Step1["<b>Action 1</b><br/><i>What happens</i>"]
    Step2["<b>Action 2</b><br/><i>What happens next</i>"]
    End["<b>End Result</b><br/><i>Final state</i>"]

    Start --> Step1
    Step1 --> Step2
    Step2 --> End

    classDef startEnd fill:#fff,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px,color:#000;
    classDef process fill:#fff,stroke:#0277bd,stroke-width:2px,color:#000;

    class Start,End startEnd;
    class Step1,Step2 process;
```

### 2. Loop or Cycle

```mermaid
graph TD
    Trigger["<b>Trigger Event</b><br/><i>What starts it</i>"]
    Action["<b>Action Taken</b><br/><i>The response</i>"]
    Result["<b>Result</b><br/><i>What happens</i>"]
    Loop["<b>Loop Back</b><br/><i>Reinforces the cycle</i>"]

    Trigger --> Action
    Action --> Result
    Result --> Loop
    Loop --> Action

    classDef trigger fill:#fff,stroke:#906,stroke-width:3px,color:#000;
    classDef loop fill:#fff,stroke:#0277bd,stroke-width:2px,stroke-dasharray: 5 5,color:#000;

    class Trigger trigger;
    class Action,Result,Loop loop;
```

### 3. Decision Tree

```mermaid
graph TD
    Question{"<b>Is condition true?</b>"}
    Yes["<b>Yes Path</b><br/><i>When true</i>"]
    No["<b>No Path</b><br/><i>When false</i>"]
    ResultYes["<b>Outcome A</b>"]
    ResultNo["<b>Outcome B</b>"]

    Question -->|Yes| Yes
    Question -->|No| No
    Yes --> ResultYes
    No --> ResultNo

    classDef decision fill:#fff,stroke:#f57c00,stroke-width:2px,color:#000;
    classDef outcome fill:#fff,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px,color:#000;

    class Question decision;
    class ResultYes,ResultNo outcome;
```

### 4. Comparison (Side-by-Side)

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph approach_a [Approach A]
        A1["<b>Step 1</b>"]
        A2["<b>Step 2</b>"]
        A3["<b>Result</b>"]
        A1 --> A2 --> A3
    end

    subgraph approach_b [Approach B]
        B1["<b>Step 1</b>"]
        B2["<b>Step 2</b>"]
        B3["<b>Result</b>"]
        B1 --> B2 --> B3
    end

    classDef groupA fill:#fff,stroke:#0277bd,stroke-width:2px,color:#000;
    classDef groupB fill:#fff,stroke:#906,stroke-width:2px,color:#000;

    class A1,A2,A3 groupA;
    class B1,B2,B3 groupB;
```

