## Checklist Before Publishing

- [ ] Does this post explain a process, loop, comparison, or hierarchy?
- [ ] Is there a concept that would be clearer visually?
- [ ] Did I add `mermaid: true` to the front matter?
- [ ] Is the diagram placed early in the post (after the hook)?
- [ ] Are node labels clear and concise (under 20 chars per line)?
- [ ] Did I use dark-mode-safe styling (white fills, colored strokes)?
- [ ] Is the node count under ~10 for readability?

---

## Good vs. Bad Diagram Choices

### Good Use Cases

+ Explaining a habit loop (trigger → action → reward → loop back)
+ Comparing two approaches side-by-side (REST vs. GraphQL structure)
+ Showing a decision tree (if X, then Y; else Z)
+ Mapping a user authentication flow (login → validate → redirect)

### Bad Use Cases

+ Simple linear lists that work better as bullet points
+ Concepts already explained clearly in one sentence
+ Over-engineering trivial processes (e.g., "Open file → Read → Close")
+ Diagrams that require more than 10 nodes (split into multiple instead)

